 Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Woodlands Ribbon Cutting & Public Open House Homecoming Spirit Week Geeks vs. Guardians 5K Fun Run Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Student Life > Veterans Services Section Navigation Bookstore & Spirit Shop Campus Life Campus Maps Dining Services Housing Safety & Security Student Activities Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources TU Library & Learning Commons Registrar Student Success Advising Tutoring Student Support Center Career Services Disability Services Student Technology Assistance Veterans Services Veterans Services +Veterans Career and Transition Center Thomas University is proud to provide services to area veterans. In April 2017, TU established the Veterans Career and Transition Center specifically for area veterans, active duty, National Guard and Reserve service members and their families. The Center provides a number of referral services to a variety of organizations who provide support and assistance to transitioning military. The Center is open to TU students and all members of the military as a resource for referrals, to relax between classes and meet with other veterans. For more information email us at military@thomasu.edu . +On Campus Counseling and Referral Services Services: Individual Counseling, Case Management, Psycho-education and Referral Services (Group Counseling upon request) Office: (850)942-8810. Thomas University has also partnered with Archbold Medical Center to provide free counseling to all students. Archbold Student Assistance Program is located at 902 Cairo Road, Thomasville, GA 31792 Phone number: 229-228-2210 OR toll free 877-237-2124Additionally, the National Suicide Prevention Lifeline is a national network of local crisis centers that provides free and confidential emotional support to people in suicidal crisis or emotional distress 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. We’re committed to improving crisis services and advancing suicide prevention by empowering individuals, advancing professional best practices, and building awareness. 1-800-273-8255 There is also a chat line available (Links to an external site.) +Student Veterans of America The mission of the SVA is to provide military veterans with the resources, support, and advocacy needed to succeed in higher education and following graduation. SVA is a 501(c)(3) coalition of student veterans groups on college campuses across the globe. These member chapters are the “boots on the ground” that help veterans reintegrate into campus life and succeed academically. Each chapter must be an officially recognized student group by their university or college and provide a peer-to-peer network for veterans who are attending the school. Additionally, chapters often coordinate campus activities, provide pre-professional networking, and generally provide a touchstone for student veterans in higher education. View the national organization’s website For more information on how you can become a Thomas University chapter member of SVA, please contact Josh Dean, Director of Military and Corporate Relations, at jdean@thomasu.edu . Questions? Call us toll free at 844-862-6978 or email us at military@thomasu.edu Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
