cation Human Resource Management (BS) Justice Administration Law Enforcement Management Medical Laboratory Science MLS 2+2, MLS Post-Baccalaureate Nursing RN-BSN, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA Psychology Rehabilitation Studies Social Work (BSW) Graduate Degrees Business Administration (MBA) Counseling Addictions, School Counseling, Mental Health, Rehabilitation Education Curriculum & Instruction, Educational Leadership, Elementary, Middle Grades, Secondary, Teacher Leadership, Master of Arts in Teaching (Initial Certification), Special Education Nursing MSN, MSN-MBA, RN-MSN, RN-MSN/MBA TU Honors Cost Tuition and Fees About Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Financial Aid Eligibility Managing Your Financial Aid Scholarships Military Tuition/Veterans Active Duty, Guard, Reserves, Veterans, DoD Civilians and military spouses Corporate Partners Student Accounts Student Life Campus Life Dining Services Housing Student Activities Safety & Security Student IDs Community Discounts Community Resources Registrar Catalog Student Handbook Course Schedule Transcripts Apply for Graduation Commencement TU Library & Learning Commons About the Library Library Policies Library FAQs Services Bookstore & Spirit Shop Book lists Bookstore Online Spirit Shop Student Support Center Career Center Disability Services Student Success Advising Tutoring Veterans Services Student Veterans of America Veterans Services and Career Transition Center Student Technology Assistance HawkLink, Email, Canvas, Password Reset, Proctor U Athletics Alumni & Friends University Advancement Meet the Team Your Gift Matters Giving Societies and Circles Endowments Impact Reports Donate Alumni Get Involved Alumni News & Events Upcoming Events Woodlands Ribbon Cutting & Public Open House Homecoming Spirit Week Geeks vs. Guardians 5K Fun Run Cairo Scholarship Soirée Dining for Education Community Resources Public & Media Relations Genealogical Library Pre-College Programs Veterans Services Ways to Give Woodlands 100 TU Annual Fund Events & Sponsorships Planned Giving About History Consumer Information Accreditation and Approvals State Authorizations Institutional Review Board Employment Faculty/Staff Technology Resources Public & Media Relations Sexual Misconduct Policy Title IX Contact Us Campus Maps Strategic Plan President's Welcome Home > Adjunct Faculty in English Composition Adjunct Faculty in English Composition DESCRIPTION: Thomas University an independent, not-for-profit, institution of higher education with undergraduate and graduate programs in Thomasville, Georgia seeks applicants for adjunct faculty in English composition. Positions are available on an as needed basis for both on-campus and online instruction. TYPICAL QUALIFICATIONS: · Candidates must hold a master’s degree or Ph.D. in the teaching discipline (English, or a related field). · Practical employment experience is preferred. · Previous teaching experience preferred but not required. · Ability to maintain confidentiality and exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with College policy · Ability to work cooperatively with all constituents · Excellent written and oral communication skills · Knowledge of course content SUPPLEMENTAL INFORMATION: All applicants must be adept in responding to student writing. To apply for opportunities, please view the Thomas University website at www.thomasu.edu/employment and click on the application link at https://apply.appone.com/job/67ddf321401b903ff3b12c1d . Also send an email with the subject noting “English Composition” including curriculum vita, three current references, and official transcripts to Anna Benefield, Office of Human Resources: abenefield@thomasu.edu. All electronic submissions should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. CONTACT INFORMATION: For questions about this faculty opening, please contact Dr. Jason Dunn at jdunn@thomasu.edu. For more information or questions regarding submission of application materials please contact Anna Benefield at abenefield@thomasu.edu. Thomas University is located in Thomasville, Georgia, approximately 35 miles north of Tallahassee, Florida. Thomas University Education that Engages ...Empowers... Transforms ™ 1550 Magnolia Street Thomasville, GA 31792 229.226.1621 Contact Us Peoples Bookstore & Spirit Shop HawkLink Student Accounts Financial Aid Campus Public & Media Relations Employment University Privacy Policy Consumer Information Website Feedback Follow Us thomas/1950/ @ThomasU1950 thomasuniversity ThomasUniversityTU © 2026 Thomas University. All Rights Reserved. Website developed and hosted by Pen Publishing Interactive"
